[h1]Yang Guang: Four Seas[/h1]
Connect cities through canals, sustain the realm through waterworks, and welcome trade from across the seas.

[h2]Sui Dynasty -- The Four Seas Connected[/h2]
[list]
[*]Imperial Seat: +2 Population and a free Granary in the Capital. Founding a city grants a Builder in that city. Relocate to a city with a Canal, up to twice.
[*]Grand Works: Engineering unlocks Canals and Dams. +50% Production toward Cisterns/Aqueducts, Canals and Dams. Canals also grant Trade Route capacity and a Trader.
[*]Flourishing Waterways: Domestic routes gain Food, Production and Gold, increasing with water infrastructure at the destination. Foreign incoming land or sea routes grant the destination +2 Gold and +1 Culture.
[*]Fertile Realm: Farms and Plantations on Grassland, Plains or Desert Floodplains gain +1 Production.
[*]Tribute of Nations: Conquering another major civilization's original Capital grants its civilization ability.
[/list]

[h2]Soldiers and Fleet[/h2]
Fubing and Xiaoguo retain their unit abilities. The Wuya Warship replaces the Frigate at Mercenaries: +5 Strength on Coast or within 2 tiles of a completed friendly Canal, and plunder protection for friendly Traders within 4 tiles.

[h2]Installation[/h2]
Adds a separate leader; original Yang Guang remains available. Requires Gathering Storm, HD, Phantagonist Yang Guang, Chinese Dynasty Uniques and their dependencies. Start a new single-player game.
Preview 0.1.3; not verified in-game. Wuya uses current Frigate base stats, costs, resources and art. The leader references the original Yang Guang portrait. Waterworks production, the founding Builder and Floodplains Production are defined independently; source-mod versions govern other inherited rules; see the bundled README for details.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Referenced abilities and resources belong to Phantagonist, HD and the official game. No third-party art is bundled. New code, documentation and cover are MIT-licensed.
